    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good point about the breathing. i'm just worried that even if i look calm, the chair might be picking up on my actual biometric signatures via skin contact or heat. do you think there are any specific types of fabric or even certain temperature adjustments i should make to my room to prevent the sensors from getting a clear reading on my body heat or heart rate?",
