      "content": "Since the chair is designed to read heat signatures, controlling the thermal environment is key to obscuring your unique biometric data. You should aim to keep your body temperature as consistent as possible, perhaps by wearing layers of clothing that help regulate heat evenly across your skin. Furthermore, slightly lowering the ambient temperature in your office might reduce the temperature differential between your body and the chair's surface, making the heat signature less distinct for any embedded sensors.",
